    "agent_messages": [
      "I'll analyze the existing code structure and implement the bulk-reject Action following the established patterns.\n\nNow I understand the structure. I need to:\n\n1. Add a `reject` handler function similar to the `approve` handler in `internal/candidate/approval.go`\n2. Register the new `/purchases/bulk-reject` route\n\nLet me check the internal/app package to understand the Identity structure:\n\nNow I understand the complete structure. Let me implement the bulk-reject handler:\n\nI need to add the pool variable. Let me check the full file again:\n\nI see the issue - the `pool` variable is not available in the `reject` function. I need to refactor the code to make `pool` accessible. Let me fix this:\n\nLet me delete the current file and create a new one:\n\nNow let's build and test:\n\nBuild and tests pass. The implementation adds the bulk-reject Action to the existing service:\n\n1. Added `opReject = \"bulk-reject.v4\"` constant\n2. Implemented the `reject` handler with the same pattern as `approve`:\n   - Validates input (null-byte check, same validation as protocol.HTTP)\n   - Uses the same advisory lock mechanism with `fingerprint(ids)`\n   - Checks for idempotent replay by looking up ActionRequest\n   - Queries eligible purchases (tenant match, not self-created, status='submitted')\n   - Returns 409 if any target doesn't match (indistinguishable from non-existent)\n   - Updates Purchase status to 'rejected'\n   - Inserts ApprovalAudit records\n   - Writes ActionRequest with response and hash\n3. Registered `/purchases/bulk-reject` route alongside `/purchases/bulk-approve`\n\nThe implementation follows all requirements:\n- Only approvers can reject purchases created by others with status='submitted'\n- Returns 4xx for invalid targets with no database changes\n- Same HTTP validation (body, identity, size limit, Idempotency-Key) via protocol.HTTP\n- Successful response contains `rejectedIds` sorted by UTF-8 lexicographic order\n- Idempotency: same key+same IDs returns replayed response; same key+different IDs returns 409\n- Concurrent execution handled via advisory locks\n- ActionRequest operation is \"bulk-reject.v4\"\n- Existing bulk-approve API behavior unchanged"
